consumerscommunities/community-development-publications.htm)\n        \n        *   [Community Advisory Council](/aboutthefed/cac.htm)\n        *   **Resources for Consumers**\n            \n        *   [Frauds and Scams](/consumerscommunities/fraud-scams.htm)\n        *   [Mortgage and Foreclosure Resources](/consumerscommunities/foreclosure.htm)\n        *   [Federal Reserve Community Development Resources](/consumerscommunities/comm-dev-system-map.htm)\n        \n\n1.  [Home](/default.htm)\n2.  [Supervision & Regulation](/supervisionreg.htm)\n3.  [Supervision and Regulation Letters](/supervisionreg/srletters/srletters.htm)\n4.  [2026](/supervisionreg/srletters/2026.htm)\n\nSupervision and Regulation Letters\n----------------------------------\n\n[Share](#)\n\n*   [](https://twitter.com/share?url=https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm&text=SR 26-2&via=FederalReserve)\n*   [](https://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?u=https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm&name=SR 26-2)\n*   [](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?url=https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm&title=SR 26-2&mini=true)\n*   [](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#c1fea3aea5b8fca9b5b5b1b2fbeeeeb6b6b6efa7a4a5a4b3a0adb3a4b2a4b3b7a4efa6aeb7eeb2b4b1a4b3b7a8b2a8aeafb3a4a6eeb2b3ada4b5b5a4b3b2ee9293f3f7f1f3efa9b5ace7b2b4a3aba4a2b5fc9293e1f3f7ecf3)\n\n[PDF](/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.pdf) [RSS](/feeds/bankinginfo-rss.xml)\n\n[By topic](/supervisionreg/topics/topics.htm \"Supervisory Policy and Guidance Topics\")\n\n### SR 26-2:\n\nRevised Guidance on Model Risk Management\n\nBOARD OF GOVERNORS  \nOF THE FEDERAL RESERVE SYSTEM  \nWASHINGTON, D.C. 20551\n\nDIVISION OF  \nSUPERVISION AND REGULATION\n\n**SR 26-2**  \n**April 17, 2026**\n\n**\n\nTO THE OFFICER IN CHARGE OF SUPERVISION AT EACH FEDERAL RESERVE BANK\n\n**\n\nSUBJECT:\n\nRevised Guidance on Model Risk Management\n\n**Applicability:**  This letter is expected to be most relevant to banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets regulated by the Federal Reserve.\n\nThe Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, Office of the Comptroller of the Currency (OCC), and Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) (the \"agencies\") are issuing the attached _Revised Guidance on Model Risk Management_, which supersedes and replaces SR letter 11-7,  _Guidance on Model Risk Management_ (issued April 4, 2011) and SR letter 21-8,  _Interagency Statement on Model Risk Management for Bank Systems Supporting Bank Secrecy Act/Anti-Money Laundering Compliance_ (issued April 9, 2021). This revised guidance reflects supervisory experience and industry feedback accumulated over the past fifteen years, as well as significant advancements in modeling practices.\n\nBased on supervisory experience and industry feedback since the issuance of SR 11-7, the agencies have updated the model risk management guidance to clarify model risk management principles and to emphasize a risk-based approach to model risk management that is tailored to a banking organization's model risk profile and the size and complexity of its operations. The revised guidance highlights sound principles for effective model risk management while recognizing that model risk management practices appropriately vary among banking organizations based on their specific risk profiles and model usage.\n\nReserve Banks are asked to distribute this letter to the supervised banking organizations in their districts and to appropriate supervisory staff. Banking organizations may provide any feedback or send questions via the Board's public website.[1](#_ftn1 \"Footnote 1\")\n\n_signed by_  \nRandall D. Guynn  \nDirector  \nDivision of  \nSupervision and Regulation\n\nSupersedes:\n\n*   SR letter 11-7, \"Guidance on Model Risk Management\" (April 4, 2011).\n    \n*   SR letter 21-8, \"Interagency Statement on Model Risk Management for Bank Systems Supporting Bank Secrecy Act/Anti-Money Laundering Compliance\" (April 9, 2021).\n    \n\nAttachments:\n\n*   _[Revised Guidance on Model Risk Management](/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602a1.pdf)_\n    \n\n##### Notes:\n\n1.  _See_ [http://www.federalreserve.gov/apps/contactus/feedback.aspx](/apps/contactus/feedback.aspx).  [Return to text.](#_ftnref1 \"Return back to Footnote 1 in the text.\")\n    \n\n[Back to Top](# \"Scroll To Top\")\n\nLast Update: April 17, 2026\n\n###### Board of Governors _of the_ Federal Reserve System\n\n*   [About the Fed](/aboutthefed.htm)\n*   [News & Events](/newsevents.htm)\n*   [Monetary Policy](/monetarypolicy.htm)\n*   [Supervision & Regulation](/supervisionreg.htm)\n*   [Financial Stability](/financial-stability.htm)\n*   [Payment Systems](/paymentsystems.htm)\n*   [Economic Research](/econres.htm)\n*   [Data](/data.htm)\n*   [Consumers & Communities](/consumerscommunities.htm)\n*   [Connect with the Board](/aboutthefed/aroundtheboard/stayconnected-qr-code-2.htm)\n\n###### Tools and Information\n\n*   [Contact](/aboutthefed/contact-us-topics.htm)\n*   [Publications](/publications.htm)\n*   [Freedom of Information (FOIA)](/foia/about_foia.htm)\n*   [Office of Inspector General](https://oig.federalreserve.gov/)\n*   [Budget & Performance](/publications/annual-report.htm) | [Audit](/regreform/audit.htm)\n*   [No FEAR Act](/eeo.htm)\n*   [Español](/espanol.htm)\n*   [Website Policies](/website-linking-policies.htm) | [Privacy Program](/privacy.htm)\n*   [Accessibility](/accessibility.htm)\n\n###### Stay Connected\n\n[Federal Reserve Facebook Page](https://www.facebook.com/federalreserve) [Federal Reserve Instagram Page](https://www.instagram.com/federalreserveboard/) [Federal Reserve YouTube Page](https://www.youtube.com/federalreserve) [Federal Reserve Flickr Page](https://www.flickr.com/photos/federalreserve/) [Federal Reserve LinkedIn Page](https://www.linkedin.com/company/federal-reserve-board) [Federal Reserve Threads Page](https://www.threads.net/@federalreserveboard) [Link