{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNbMx8Mq2G227PuhFGbL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JaacrJruufLeGHkKA1yChd","name":"mcp__week1-wire__check_claims","input":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Jordan Reyes (fictional), the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, revised model risk management guidance that supersedes SR 11-7 and SR 21-8. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter asks for a risk-based approach tailored to each banking organization's model risk profile, size and complexity. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets regulated by the Federal Reserve. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 describes a model inventory as the system of record and calls for monitoring of autonomous decision making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 sets technology and cyber risk expectations for federally regulated financial institutions. [src-osfi-b13]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group (fictional) has a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve; the letter addresses those organizations and is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion in total assets, so applicability requires confirmation. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group (fictional) has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n- A Canadian domestic systemically important bank with about $900 billion (USD) in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- The bank already runs Forge. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Agents are in production and the bank has a risk committee. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n- The record does not show whether it has a Federal Reserve-regulated US entity. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- Reign Assurance is in co-design development. [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n- The assurance and reliance judgments stay with your business, risk, compliance and audit experts, and any audit opinion or certification stays with their auditors. [P-RELIANCE]\n\n## Suggested next step\nJordan offers the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how the agents already in production would sit in an E-23 model inventory, once the Federal Reserve question is answered.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n- Does Northbridge have a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve, and what are its total assets?\n- Does it have EU entities of a type DORA covers?\n- Which production agents run on Forge, and are they in the model inventory today?\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\nRisk: E-23 takes effect May 1, 2027 and names AI and machine learning models, and Northbridge already has agents in production. The question for model risk and audit is whether those agents are inventoried and monitored, and what evidence the risk committee would see.\n\nEngineering: The agents run on the Forge estate Northbridge already operates. The question for platform engineering is how agent calls to models and tools reach an approved, logged path that model risk can review.\n\n## Sources\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-osfi-e23] OSFI Guideline E-23 - Model Risk Management (2027) - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/guideline-e-23-model-risk-management-2027\n- [src-osfi-b13] OSFI Guideline B-13 - Technology and Cyber Risk Management - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/technology-cyber-risk-management\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1001] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001] Clay enrichment row\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-RELIANCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3080,"cache_read_input_tokens":38277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3080},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f0686f-6b6a-4bca-80e3-d1af26120d40","uuid":"fb188da3-1b8b-4124-9d74-8e436637607c","timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:39:03.374Z","request_id":"req_011CfNbMw9LGvVmCPtt7w6zj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JaacrJruufLeGHkKA1yChd":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Jordan Reyes (fictional), the account owner, to decide whether to share it in th