{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNbQRQkCEgv2UhE1YgP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gate fills in recipients from route_contact, and it included the CISO (zi-2005). I'll come back to that. First I'm fixing the length, the Forge mentions and the missing Sources entries."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5990,"cache_read_input_tokens":41357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5990},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f0686f-6b6a-4bca-80e3-d1af26120d40","uuid":"7a56e607-3b31-4109-982a-da48be918756","timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:39:10.927Z","request_id":"req_011CfNbQQsF42kM1bUpoZk1w"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNbQRQkCEgv2UhE1YgP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YEq2KZSCFwAjDPzWRnkzPq","name":"mcp__week1-wire__check_claims","input":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Jordan Reyes (fictional), the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, revised model risk management guidance that supersedes SR 11-7 and SR 21-8. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets regulated by the Federal Reserve. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 treats the model inventory as the system of record and calls for monitoring of autonomous decision making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 sets technology and cyber risk expectations for federally regulated financial institutions. [src-osfi-b13]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group (fictional) has a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve; the letter addresses those organizations and is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion in total assets, so applicability requires confirmation. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group (fictional) has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n- A Canadian domestic systemically important bank with about $900 billion (USD) in total assets, in an existing customer relationship. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Agents are in production, the bank has a risk committee, and a Federal Reserve-regulated US entity is not on record. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- Reign Assurance is in co-design development. [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n\n## Suggested next step\nJordan offers the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how its production agents would sit in an E-23 model inventory.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n- Does Northbridge have a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve, and what are its total assets?\n- Does it have EU entities of a type DORA covers?\n- Which production agents run on the platform we operate with them, and are they in the model inventory today?\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\nRisk: E-23 takes effect May 1, 2027 and names AI and machine learning models, and Northbridge already has agents in production. The question for model risk and audit is whether those agents are inventoried and monitored, and what evidence the risk committee would see.\n\nEngineering: The agents already run in production. The question for platform engineering is how agent calls to models and tools reach an approved, logged path that model risk can review.\n\n## Sources\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-osfi-e23] OSFI Guideline E-23 - Model Risk Management (2027) - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/guideline-e-23-model-risk-management-2027\n- [src-osfi-b13] OSFI Guideline B-13 - Technology and Cyber Risk Management - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/technology-cyber-risk-management\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1001] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2005] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5990,"cache_read_input_tokens":41357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5990},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f0686f-6b6a-4bca-80e3-d1af26120d40","uuid":"41d7cfe6-d3c8-41a9-aac8-f66f17fcdcf9","timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:39:21.979Z","request_id":"req_011CfNbQQsF42kM1bUpoZk1w","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YEq2KZSCFwAjDPzWRnkzPq":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1001","brief_markdown":"# Northbridge Financial Group (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Jordan Reyes (fictional), the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, revised model risk management guidance that supersedes SR 11-7 and SR 21-8. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets regulated by the Federal Reserve. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n- OSFI Guideline E-23 covers model risk, including AI and machine learning models, and takes effect on May 1, 2027. [src-osfi-e23]\n- E-23 treats the model inventory as the system of record and calls for monitoring of autonomous decision making and model drift. [src-osfi-e23]\n- OSFI Guideline B-13 sets technology and cyber risk expectations for federally regulated financial institutions. [src-osfi-b13]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group (fictional) has a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve; the letter addresses those organizations and is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion in total assets, so applicability requires confirmation. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Northbridge Financial Group (fictional) has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n- A Canadian domestic systemically important bank with about $900 billion (USD) in total assets, in an existing customer relationship. [hubspot:company/hs-1001]\n- Agents are in production, the bank has a risk committee, and a Federal Reserve-regulated US entity is not on record. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- Reign Assurance is in co-design development. [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n\n## Suggested next step\nJordan offers the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on how its production agents would sit in an E-23 model inventory.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n- Does Northbridge have a US banking organization regulated by the Federal Reserve, and what are its total assets?\n- Does it have EU entities of a type DORA covers?\n- Which production agents run on the platform we operate with them, and are they in the model inventory today?\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\nRisk: E-23 takes effect May 1, 2027 and names AI and machine learning models, and Northbridge already has agents in production. The question for model risk and audit is whether those agents are inventoried and monitored, and what evidence the risk committee would see.\n\nEngineering: The agents already run in production. The question for platform engineering is how agent calls to models and tools reach an approved, logged path that model risk can review.\n\n## Sources\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-osfi-e23] OSFI Guideline E-23 - Model Risk Management (2027) - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/guideline-e-23-model-risk-management-2027\n- [src-osfi-b13] OSFI Guideline B-13 - Technology and Cyber Risk Management - https://www.osfi-bsif.gc.ca/en/guidance/guidance-library/technology-cyber-risk-management\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1001] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1001] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2001] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2002] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2003] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2004] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2005] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance"}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YEq2KZSCFwAjDPzWRnkzPq","display_name":"Check Claims","server_display_name":"week1-wire"}]}
