{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNbS9NQLZodaMcxshYdF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VeLzQM6u1FaSy21Wi2iZcz","name":"mcp__week1-wire__check_claims","input":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1002","brief_markdown":"# Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Jordan Reyes (fictional), the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, revised model risk management guidance that supersedes SR 11-7 and SR 21-8. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter asks for a risk-based approach tailored to each banking organization's model risk profile, size and complexity. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets regulated by the Federal Reserve. [src-sr26-2]\n- The record shows a Federal Reserve-regulated entity and about $85 billion (USD) in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1002] [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional)'s banking organizations are regulated by the Federal Reserve, and their total assets; the letter is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional) has EU entities of the types DORA (Regulation (EU) 2022/2554) covers; per EIOPA, 20 types of financial entities plus ICT third-party providers, so it depends on entity type, jurisdiction and facts. [src-dora]\n\n## What we know about the account\n- A US bank holding company with about 12,000 employees. [hubspot:company/hs-1002]\n- Agent adoption is planned, not yet in production, and the bank has a risk committee. [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002]\n\n## Where Reign fits\n- Reign Gateway gives applications and agents a governed path to approved models and tools. [P-GATEWAY]\n- Reign prepares the evidence; the people who own the risk decide. [P-EVIDENCE]\n- Reign Assurance is in co-design development. [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS]\n\n## Suggested next step\nJordan offers the audit and risk committee an Executive Assurance Briefing on bringing planned agents under the model risk program before they reach production.\n\n## Suggested recipients in the existing relationship\n\n## Open questions for the account owner\n- Which of Lakeshore's banking organizations are Federal Reserve-regulated, and how does its model risk program read SR 26-2 against SR 11-7?\n- Does it have EU entities of a type DORA covers?\n- Which agent use cases are planned, and when do they reach production?\n\n## Lane framings for the account owner\nRisk: SR 26-2 replaces SR 11-7, the reference Lakeshore's model risk program has likely been built on. With agents still planned, the question for the Chief Risk Officer is how agents enter the model inventory and what evidence the risk committee sees before launch.\n\nEngineering: Agents are planned, not yet built. The question for AI engineering is how agent calls to models and tools will reach an approved, logged path that model risk can review from day one.\n\n## Sources\n- [src-sr26-2] Federal Reserve SR 26-2 - https://www.federalreserve.gov/supervisionreg/srletters/SR2602.htm\n- [src-dora] EIOPA - Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) - https://www.eiopa.europa.eu/digital-operational-resilience-act-dora_en\n- [hubspot:company/hs-1002] HubSpot company record\n- [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002] Clay enrichment row\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2006] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [zoominfo:contact/zi-2007] ZoomInfo contact record\n- [P-GATEWAY] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/gateway\n- [P-EVIDENCE] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance\n- [P-ASSURANCE-STATUS] iTmethods - https://itmethods.com/assurance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":607,"cache_read_input_tokens":51151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":607},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f0686f-6b6a-4bca-80e3-d1af26120d40","uuid":"84afe9a0-907c-4854-966c-e463a6c53a56","timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:39:40.586Z","request_id":"req_011CfNbS8tdEj663GZf7Shu2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VeLzQM6u1FaSy21Wi2iZcz":{"playbook_id":"bank-sr26-2","account_id":"hs-1002","brief_markdown":"# Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional): SR 26-2 brief for the account owner\n\nPrepared for Jordan Reyes (fictional), the account owner, to decide whether to share it in the existing relationship. Nothing has been sent and the bank has not been contacted.\n\n## What changed\n- On April 17, 2026 the Federal Reserve, with the OCC and FDIC, issued SR 26-2, revised model risk management guidance that supersedes SR 11-7 and SR 21-8. [src-sr26-2]\n- The letter asks for a risk-based approach tailored to each banking organization's model risk profile, size and complexity. [src-sr26-2]\n\n## What is certain for this account\n- The letter expects to be most relevant to banking organizations with over $30 billion in total assets regulated by the Federal Reserve. [src-sr26-2]\n- The record shows a Federal Reserve-regulated entity and about $85 billion (USD) in total assets. [hubspot:company/hs-1002] [clay:table/first-motion/row/hs-1002]\n\n## What depends on structure (confirm)\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp (fictional)'s banking organizations are regulated by the Federal Reserve, and their total assets; the letter is expected to be most relevant above $30 billion. [src-sr26-2]\n- Confirm: whether Lakeshore Bancorp (fic