{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNbU1H2psueRpVdsnphF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran all three accounts. One brief went to the account owner for approval, one is held, and one is closed. Nothing was sent to anyone.\n\n| Account | Outcome | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| hs-1002 Lakeshore Bancorp | **Brief written, awaiting approval from Jordan Reyes** | Screening included it, and the applicability check said \"ready\". The record shows a Federal Reserve-regulated entity and $85B in total assets. |\n| hs-1001 Northbridge Financial Group | **Held by me; draft passed the claims gate but I did not submit it** | route_contact put the CISO on the recipient list. Details below. |\n| hs-1010 Riverbend Credit Union | **Closed, marked do-not-contact** | 800 employees is under the 5,000 floor. screen_account recorded the exclusion. |\n\n**Lakeshore output**\n- Brief: `briefs/hubspot_company_hs-1002.md`\n- Approval request: `.../approvals/hubspot_company_hs-1002.json`\n- Review page: `.../review.html`\n- Jordan decides with `python3 -m agent.feedback.decide --request <approval json>`\n\n**Why Northbridge is held**\n- route_contact returned Sofia Marchetti, the Chief Information Security Officer, in the risk lane. The tool says it never returns do-not-route titles, and the run rules say the CISO is never routed.\n- The claims gate fills the recipients section from that routing, so submitting would have put the CISO on the brief. I couldn't remove her without working around the tool, so I recorded a hold with that reason instead.\n- This looks like a routing bug in the tools, not a problem with the account. Once routing is fixed, the Northbridge draft can go through again. It already passes the gate and includes the required phrase \"applicability requires confirmation\". Its OSFI E-23 and B-13 lines are stated as certain for a Canadian bank.\n\n**Other notes**\n- **Source reading:** WebFetch isn't directly available in this session, so I used the web-fetch agent, which uses WebFetch. All four source pages loaded.\n- **SR 26-2 detail:** the letter's attached PDF, which holds the detailed guidance, came back unreadable. So the briefs only state what the cover letter says: it replaces SR 11-7 and SR 21-8, calls for a risk-based approach, and is most relevant above $30B. Neither brief mentions AI in relation to SR 26-2.\n- **Lakeshore wording:** even though the tool rated SR 26-2 as \"applies\" for Lakeshore, the brief never says the rule applies. Federal Reserve status and total assets are still listed as items to confirm. I also removed an unsourced guess from the risk-lane framing before submitting.\n- **Scoring:** I didn't run `python3 -m evals.score_run`, because you limited this run to the week1-wire tools and WebFetch. I can run it if you want the scores."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2002,"cache_read_input_tokens":54853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2002},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f0686f-6b6a-4bca-80e3-d1af26120d40","uuid":"1c01fb59-2980-41e2-9694-c35cb32a89d4","timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:40:02.241Z","request_id":"req_011CfNbTzmnAouga33ypxBpA"}
